# Convergence orders of trapezoid, Simpson and 4-node Gauss–Legendre quadrature

**Setup.** How fast do three composite rules converge on [0, 1], and does the order match theory (2, 4, 8)? Integrands exp(x) (exact e−1), 1/(1+25x²) (exact atan(5)/5) and √x (exact 2/3). Rules: composite trapezoid; composite Simpson with *n* panels, each using its endpoints and midpoint (2*n* subintervals); Gauss–Legendre with *n* panels × 4 nodes (`numpy.polynomial.legendre.leggauss`). *n* = 2^k, k = 1…12; double precision; error = |computed − exact|. Order = −slope of an ordinary least-squares fit of ln(error) on ln(*n*) over points with error > 10⁻¹⁵ (about 4.5 ε; the integrals are O(1)); 95 % interval = slope ± t₀.₉₇₅,ₘ₋₂·SE for *m* fitted points. Numbers: `experiment-repo` `results/` (`errors.csv`, `fits.csv`, `supplement.json`).

